        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "Root sheet: XOR gate (74LVC...) with pins 1=Troj_XOR_A, 2=Troj_XOR_B, 4=Troj_XOR_Y, 5=VCC, 3=GND (controller.kicad_sch, page 1)"},
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "mcu sheet: U6 pin 5 DELAY -> Troj_XOR_Y; U1 pin 5 GPIO02 -> Troj_XOR_A (mcu.kicad_sch, page 3)"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "Heater path: 'IN/DIAG_EN (pins 1/2) are both driven from ESP32 GPIO1 ... CL (pin 4) and GND (pin 6) and the exposed pad EP (pin 9) all go to GND, and ~{FAULT} (pin 3) is broken out to test point TP6 only.' (no DELAY driven by a gate; no 74LVC part in component table)"}
      ],
      "impact": "A hidden logic gate modulates the TPS1H200 heater switch DELAY pin from a free GPIO and a thermocouple line, allowing heater on/off timing to be altered independent of the documented bang-bang control — consistent with deliberate tampering (a hardware trojan).",
      "confidence": 0.9
    },
    {
      "category": "bridged_nets",
      "components": ["U4", "J3", "74LVC1G86 XOR gate (root sheet)"],
      "pins": ["U4.2", "J3.1"],
      "nets": ["Troj_XOR_B"],
      "observed": "On the thermocouples sheet (page 5) the U4 pin 2 (T-) / J3 pin 1 net carries the label 'Troj_XOR_B', the same name as the XOR gate's input B on the root sheet (page 1), so the zone-3 thermocouple negative input is merged with a logic-gate input net.",
      "expected": "Per spec, T- (pin 2) of each MAX31855 is wired directly to its screw terminal as a dedicated differential thermocouple input, shared with no other signal.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "thermocouples sheet: U4 pin 2 T- / J3 pin 1 labeled Troj_XOR_B (thermocouples.kicad_sch, page 5)"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "Thermocouple wire pair connects to a 2-pin screw terminal ... whose two pins wire directly to the MAX31855's differential thermocouple inputs T+ (pin 3) and T- (pin 2)."}
      ],
      "impact": "Loading the thermocouple-3 negative input with a logic gate corrupts the zone-3 temperature measurement and supplies the trojan gate with a sensor-derived input.",
      "confidence": 0.8
    }
  ],
  "summary": "Anomaly detected: the drawing contains an undocumented 74LVC1G86 XOR gate with nets named 'Troj_XOR_*' whose output drives the heater switch DELAY pin and whose inputs come from GPIO02 and the U4 thermocouple T- line — a hardware trojan not present in the specification, which also bridges a thermocouple sense net into a logic net."
}

